ineering and Machinery</publisher-name><fpage>76</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004856-United1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific</collab><year>1984</year><source>Updated guidebook on biogas development</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>United Nations</publisher-name><fpage>xi, 178</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004856-VanBuren1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Buren</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1979</year><source>A Chinese biogas manual : popularising technology in the countryside</source><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Intermediate Technology Pub</publisher-name><fpage>135</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004856-Gunnerson1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gunnerson</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuckey</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><source>Anaerobic digestion : principles and practices for biogas systems</source><publisher-loc>Washington, D.C., U.S.A.</publisher-loc><publisher-name>World Bank</publisher-name><fpage>xv, 154</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004856-Arnott1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Arnott</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1984</year><source>The biogas/biofertilizer business handbook : a handbook for volunteers</source><publisher-loc>Washington, D.C.</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Peace Corps, Information Collection and Exchange</publisher-name><fpage>ix, 171</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0004856-Subramanian1"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>